    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d566">

                <pb facs="0646" n="572" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg572"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 701.6261/11</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul at Moscow</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Poole</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi><anchor
                        n="2" xml:id="d566-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-07-06T19:00:00+04:31">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 6, 1918, 7 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received July 9, 4.10 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>702. Urgent for Secretary’s attention. Smith of the Associated Press has just
                    learned from an authoritative source that the German Ambassador, Count Mirbach,
                    was assassinated between 2 and 3 this afternoon at his Embassy. Two persons
                    arriving in machine threw bomb through window. Ambassador and Captain König
                    wounded. Ambassador died in few minutes. Two arrests so far. Smith asks that
                    Associated Press be informed.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Poole</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d566-f1" n="2" type="source" xml:id="d566-f1-content">
                <p>Sent via the Embassy in France (No. 4411); by wireless from Moscow to Paris.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
